{block title}Rules{/block}

{block main}
<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h1>Rules of the FYKOS Correspondence Competition</h1>
        <p>On this page you will find the full text of the rules for the FYKOS Correspondence Competition.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary my-2" n:href=":Events:Fykos:default">Basic Information About the Competition</a>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Registration</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Participation in the FYKOS Correspondence Competition (hereinafter referred to as "FYKOS") requires
                prior registration in the submission system at <a href="https://db.fykos.cz/">https://db.fykos.cz/</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                By registering for FYKOS, a participant confirms that they have read these Rules and undertakes to
                follow them.
            </li>
            <li>FYKOS is an individual competition.</li>
            <li>
                Each participant must be a high-school student, a primary-school student, or their respective
                equivalent.
            </li>
            <li>
                It is possible to register for a given year of the competition at any time during its course, but no
                later than the submission deadline of the last series.
            </li>
            <li>
                Participants are obliged to provide truthful information upon registration and, should it change, to
                update it or notify the organizers of the change without undue delay.
            </li>
            <li>
                By registering for the competition, a participant agrees to the publication of their results in the form
                of basic information (their name, surname, category, school, and points) in the results list in both
                print and digital outputs.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Designation into Categories</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                The competition is held in four categories, which correspond to the four years of high school study,
                that is, study at level 3 of the ISCED 2011 classification. In the Czech Republic, this typically means
                a four-year high school.
            </li>
            <li>
                A participant is assigned to a category based on their expected school year of high school graduation. A
                participant who is, at the time of the competition, in the final (i.e., graduating) year of high school
                competes in the 4th-year category. A participant in the penultimate year competes in the 3rd-year
                category, and so on.
            </li>
            <li>
                Pupils of primary schools and of the corresponding lower years of multi-year grammar schools are
                assigned to the 1st-year category.
            </li>
            <li>
                In ambiguous cases, a participant's category is determined by the head organizer or an organizer
                authorized by them. The organizers reserve the right to adjust a participant's assignment to a category
                if they find that the information provided upon registration is inaccurate.
            </li>
            <li>All categories share the same set of problems.</li>
            <li>Each category has its own results list.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Competition Format</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>One year of FYKOS consists of six series, each of which contains eight problems.</li>
            <li>
                Each series contains two easy theoretical problems, three difficult theoretical problems, one open
                problem, one experimental problem, and one serial problem.
            </li>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    The statement of the open problem is typically open-ended and calls for a detailed physical analysis
                    of the situation posed.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The experimental problem requires carrying out the assigned experiment and processing the measured
                    data.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The serial problems within a single year are all devoted to a single, more advanced topic. Each
                    serial problem is published together with an installment of the serial, an instructional text that
                    introduces the theory needed to solve the problem.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <li>
                Problem statements are published progressively, series by series, in the
                <a n:href=":Default:Problems:">Problems section</a> of the website
                <a href="https://fykos.org/">https://fykos.org/</a> (hereinafter referred to as the "FYKOS website").
            </li>
            <li>
                If a serious issue is found in the statement of a problem, the organizers reserve the right to modify
                that problem or eliminate it from the competition, without any entitlement to compensation. Participants
                will be informed of such changes on the main page of the FYKOS website.
            </li>
            <li>
                In the case of a less serious error in a problem statement or an issue in the grading or the results,
                the organizers reserve the right to make an appropriate correction. Such changes will be made on the
                relevant pages of the FYKOS website, and the participants concerned may be informed of them
                individually.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2 id="solution-requirements">Solution Requirements</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                The competition languages are Czech, Slovak, and English. Solutions written in any other language will
                not be graded.
            </li>
            <li>
                The maximum length of the solution to a single problem is 12 standard pages (approx. 21,600 characters).
                Parts of a solution exceeding this limit need not be taken into account.
            </li>
            <li>
                Every solution must include a clearly explained line of reasoning, not merely the result. The reasoning
                must make clear which physical considerations and assumptions the participant used and which key steps
                of the derivation they carried out.
            </li>
            <li>
                For an experimental problem, the solution must further include a description of the apparatus used, the
                measurement procedure, the measured data, and an evaluation of the measurement uncertainties; more
                detailed methodological instructions are given in the
                <a n:href=":experiments">Guide to FYKOS Experimental Problems</a>, available on the FYKOS website.
            </li>
            <li>
                When solving the problems, participants are permitted to use any literature and any internet sources.
                When using someone else's texts, figures, data, calculations, procedures, or other materials, the
                participant must properly cite the source. Verbatim reproduction of passages is admissible only to a
                reasonable extent and with a proper citation of the source.
            </li>
            <li>A participant must work out the solution to each problem independently.</li>
            <li>
                Minor consultations about the problems with other participants, teachers, and other people are
                permitted. A consultation must not amount to handing over a complete solution to a problem or a
                substantial part of it, systematically guiding the participant step by step, or having another person
                work out key parts of the solution.
            </li>
            <li>
                It is forbidden to present someone else's solution as one's own. This prohibition applies both to
                copying from other participants and to solutions, or substantial parts thereof, produced by another
                person or by a generative artificial intelligence tool, even if the source is cited.
            </li>
            <li>
                Generative artificial intelligence tools must not solve a problem for a participant or write up the
                solution. The use of these tools is governed by the <a n:href=":aiRules">Rules on the Use of AI</a>,
                available on the FYKOS website.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Submission of Solutions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Solutions are submitted through the submission system at
                <a href="https://db.fykos.cz/">https://db.fykos.cz/</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                The only accepted format is PDF in A4 size. A solution may be written up electronically, or it may be a
                scan of a handwritten solution. A scan of a handwritten solution must be legible and correctly oriented.
                Submitting a solution in any other format creates a risk that the solution or a part of it will be lost,
                for which the organizers accept no responsibility.
            </li>
            <li>The maximum size of a submitted file is 30 MB.</li>
            <li>
                The solution to each problem is submitted as a separate file; solutions to multiple problems cannot be
                combined into a single PDF.
            </li>
            <li>
                The first page of every solution must clearly state the problem number, the series number, and the
                participant's name. If a solution has more than one page, the participant's name must appear on each of
                them.
            </li>
            <li>
                A participant may submit solutions to any number of problems from a given series; it is not necessary to
                submit all of them. Individual problems may be submitted independently of one another.
            </li>
            <li>
                If a participant submits a solution to the same problem more than once, the last version submitted
                before the submission deadline is graded.
            </li>
            <li>
                Solutions must be submitted no later than the deadline stated for the given series. The official
                submission time is the timestamp recorded by the submission system. Solutions submitted after the
                deadline will not be graded, unless the organizers decide otherwise.
            </li>
            <li>
                The organizers reserve the right to postpone the submission deadline of a problem or of an entire
                series. Participants will be informed of such a change on the main page of the FYKOS website.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Grading and Awarding of Points</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>The maximum score for each problem is given in its problem statement.</li>
            <li>
                Solutions are graded by designated graders. The grading assesses both the correctness of a solution and
                its compliance with the <a href="#solution-requirements">Solution Requirements</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                Partial solutions are graded as well; points are awarded for individual steps and considerations, not
                only for arriving at the correct result.
            </li>
            <li>
                For particularly high-quality solutions — for example, exceptionally original ones, unusually thorough
                ones, or ones that show deep physical insight — graders may award bonus points beyond the maximum score
                for the problem. The award of bonus points is a matter of the grader's expert judgment; there is no
                entitlement to bonus points.
            </li>
            <li>
                Solutions, or parts of them, need not be graded if they are illegible, written in a language other than
                a competition language, submitted after the deadline, or if they otherwise violate the
                <a href="#solution-requirements">Solution Requirements</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                After the grading of a given series is complete, participants can view their graded solutions in the
                submission system at <a href="https://db.fykos.cz/">https://db.fykos.cz/</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                If participants have any questions or comments regarding their graded solutions, they may contact the
                organizers at the email address
                <a href="mailto:fykos@fykos.org">fykos@fykos.org</a>. The period for submitting comments is at
                least 14 days from the date on which the graded solutions of the last series are made available; the
                organizers will announce the exact deadline to participants via the email address provided upon
                registration. Comments will be considered and, where appropriate, reflected in the grading.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Competition Results and Prizes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>After each series has been graded, the current results lists are published on the FYKOS website.</li>
            <li>
                The overall ranking in each category is determined by the participants' total score across all series of
                the given year. Participants with an equal total score share the same rank.
            </li>
            <li>
                For participants in the 1st-year and 2nd-year categories, the points earned for problems 1 and 2 in each
                series count double in the results lists. No other point advantages apply.
            </li>
            <li>
                A successful solver is a participant who, in a given year, obtains at least half of the maximum number
                of points attainable in the 4th-year category (bonus points not included).
            </li>
            <li>
                The best participants may be rewarded, for example, with material prizes or with the opportunity to take
                part in some of the FYKOS events. Participants have no entitlement to material prizes or to any other
                rewards.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2 id="breach-of-rules">Breach of Rules</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                In the case of a breach of these Rules, or of a reasonable suspicion of such a breach, the organizers
                may take this into account in the grading.
            </li>
            <li>
                Depending on the seriousness of the situation, the organizers may reduce the score of the solution
                concerned, not grade the solution concerned, remove points that have already been awarded, disqualify
                the participant from the competition, or restrict their participation in subsequent years of the
                competition or in other FYKOS events. The organizers also reserve the right to share information about
                rule violations with the organizers of other competitions and activities organized or promoted by the
                CUNI MFF, as well as with representatives of the participants' schools.
            </li>
            <li>
                Measures taken in response to a breach of these Rules are decided on by the head organizer or an
                organizer authorized by them.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<div class="panel color-auto">
    <section class="inner-container">
        <h2>Final Remarks</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                The organizers reserve the right to make minor changes and clarifications to these Rules during the
                course of a year. Participants will be informed of any such changes on the FYKOS website.
            </li>
            <li>
                Any disputes and difficulties that are not covered by these Rules are decided on by the head organizer
                or an organizer authorized by them.
            </li>
            <li>These Rules were approved by the organizers of FYKOS and come into effect on September 1, 2026.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
